#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:2
msgid "Native Instruments Traktor Kontrol S4 MK3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:4
msgid ""
"The Kontrol S4 MK3 is a 4 deck all-in-one controller with a sturdy build "
"quality and integrated sound card. Compared to the MK2 and MK1, it also has "
"shiny, motorised aluminum jogwheels, screens and a set of pads which can be "
"used for various features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:8
msgid ""
"The S4 MK3 uses the standard :term:`HID` protocol for the buttons, knobs, "
"faders and LEDs, and extends it for the motorized jogwheels. The screens use"
" a USB Bulk transfer. The easiest way to tell the MK3 apart from the MK1 and"
" Mk2 models are these screens, placed in between the \"Move\" and \"Loop\" "
"encoders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:12
msgid ""
"Unlike its predecessors, the Kontrol S4 Mk3 cannot run from :term:`USB` "
"power and the separate power supply must be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:14
msgid ""
"`Manufacturer’s product page <https://www.native-"
"instruments.com/en/products/traktor/dj-controllers/traktor-kontrol-s4/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:17
msgid "Added support for screens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:19
msgid "Added beatjump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:21
msgid "Added stems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:25
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:27
msgid ""
"The Kontrol S4 MK3 is a USB class compliant audio and :term:`HID`, so it is "
"compatible with Mixxx without any proprietary drivers on GNU/Linux, MacOS "
"and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:29
msgid ""
"With the S4 plugged in, a HID device is listed as an available controller in"
" Mixxx’s Preferences. The controller uses HID for each components on the "
"device, except the screens, so the mapping can only be loaded when you "
"select the HID device on the left side of Mixxx’s Preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:33
msgid "Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:36
msgid "Setup audio output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:39
msgid "Using the S4 mixer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:41
msgid ""
"In order to use the audio output of the controller, select the device "
":guilabel:`Traktor Kontrol S4 MK3`. :guilabel:`Channels 1 - 2` should be set"
" as :guilabel:`Main` and :guilabel:`Channels 3 - 4` should be set as "
":guilabel:`Headphones`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:44
msgid "Using the software mixer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:46
msgid ""
"If you don't want to use certain outputs of the device, you can enable the "
"mapping of the mixer knob to the Mixxx internal mixer. Head over to the "
":ref:`settings` to enable these optional mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:48
msgid ""
"The mixer knobs are physically linked to the S4 embedded mixer. This means "
"that there is no way to prevent these buttons to adjust gains of the output,"
" and will lead to unexpected volume mixing if the Mixxx mixer is used while "
"also using S4 outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:52
msgid "Known bugs and limitation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:55
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:57
msgid ""
"During the development phase, it appears that using other Sound API than "
"`ALSA` would lead the Master VU meter not to work. Furthermore, audio output"
" power would be half as loud as it should be, which can be a problem if you "
"are also using other software, since you audio setting will suddenly become "
"twice as loud. It remains unclear whether or not this was a common issue or "
"if this was specific to the used setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:62
msgid "Screens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:64
msgid ""
"The controller screens are supported, but they require a little bit of "
"tinkering. Due to the legacy controller engine, the screen are driven by a "
"separate mapping, which will have to be set independently of the controller "
"mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:67
msgid ""
"The screens rendering is done using QML and the communication is achieved "
"via BULK USB endpoint. Both of these features are not available out of the "
"box on Windows and Mac for now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:69
msgid ""
"By default, the screens are standalone. This means that local state changes "
"such as deck selection or shifting will not trigger any screen interaction, "
"and thus you should expect only Deck A and B to be displayed on these screen"
" by default, although this can be changed in the controller settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:72
msgid ""
"It exists an API that was temporarily parked that allows mappings to "
"communicate. If you want, you may `download pre-built binaries "
"<https://github.com/acolombier/mixxx/actions/runs/13751974244?pr=10>` or "
"build a version of Mixxx with `this feature "
"<https://github.com/acolombier/mixxx/pull/10>` and it should automatically "
"work on the controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:77
msgid "Motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:79
msgid ""
"Haptic feedback (know as Haptic Drive (TM)) is partially implemented. "
"Supported features include jogwheel tensions and turntable mode, but these "
"features remain in beta and may sometime have unexpected behaviours. Since "
"there is no guarantee on the long term effect to the controller of how Mixxx"
" implements these features, they are disabled by default. You can enable "
"them by setting `UseMotors` to `true` in :ref:`settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:85
msgid "Mapping Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:90
msgid "Jogwheel modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:92
msgid ""
"The jogwheel can be used to control various things, depending on the mode "
"they are in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:94
msgid ""
"**Vinyl mode** (*default*): The jogwheel platter can be used for scratch. "
"The jogwheel crown can be used to jog up or down the playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:95
msgid ""
"**Jog mode**: The wheel platter and crown can be used to jog up or down the "
"playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:96
msgid ""
"**Turntable mode**: The wheel behaves as a 33.3 RPM turntable. If the "
"platter or crown are slowed down or speeded up, then it will scratch down or"
" up the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:98
msgid ""
"Because this mode relies on Mixxx's scratch mode, if the track has been "
"pitched up, the keylock will be ignored!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:100
msgid ""
"This mode is only available if the motor features are enabled. See "
":ref:`use-motors` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:102
msgid ""
"**Loop in**: The wheel behaves similarly to CDJ. If the platter or crown are"
" turned, it will move back or forth the start of the loop. Additionally, if "
"the loop encoder is used, it will move the all loop back or forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/native_instruments_traktor_kontrol_s4_mk3.rst:103
msgid ""
"**Loop out**: Like the **Loop in** mode, but for the exit position of the "
"loop. If the platter or crown are turned, it will move the end of the loop "
"back or forth. Additionally, the \"Loop\" encoder can used in the same way "
"as in **Loop in** mode."
msgstr ""

